      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(zalo): bound proxy fetcher cache to 64 entries",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Zalo `resolveZaloProxyFetch` retained one `makeProxyFetch` entry per distinct proxy URL in a process-lifetime `Map` with no eviction. Config churn or high-cardinality proxy URLs could therefore grow gateway memory without a hard bound.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Cap `proxyCache` at 64 entries using the shared `pruneMapToMaxSize` helper after every successful insert (same pattern as Nextcloud Talk room cache / MS Teams team-group cache / Mattermost opaque-target cache).\n- Insertion-order eviction keeps newest proxy fetchers; cache-hit identity and empty-URL behavior are unchanged.\n- Adds a focused regression that fills `max+1` distinct URLs, proves the oldest entry is rebuilt on next use, and confirms a mid-window entry still hits.\n\nNo new config/env surface. Does not change Bot API timeouts (`#104017`) or other Zalo send paths.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** Long-running Zalo gateways could retain an unbounded number of proxy fetcher closures as distinct proxy URLs appeared.\n\n**After:** At most 64 distinct proxy fetchers are retained; older ones are dropped and rebuilt on next use.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCompete: no open PR for `extensions/zalo/src/proxy.ts` / `proxyCache` bounding.\n\nHead: `bad401574df2f33ad584b94618fac8de3e45ad28`\n\n```text\n$ OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/zalo/src/proxy.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n[zalo proxyCache proof] max=64 filled=65 oldest_evicted=true rebuilt=true mid_hit=true\n ✓ returns undefined for empty or whitespace proxy URLs\n ✓ caches fetchers by trimmed proxy URL\n ✓ evicts the oldest proxy fetcher when more than 64 distinct URLs are resolved\n ✓ evicts an early entry when newer distinct proxies fill the cache\nTests  4 passed (4)\n```\n\nNegative control: without `pruneMapToMaxSize`, resolving proxy-0 after 65 fills would reuse the original fetcher identity; with the cap, proxy-0 rebuilds (`makeProxyFetch` call count increases) while a mid-window URL still hits.",
